nodecode-maqami-travel is a rewrite of negm17111995's negm17111995/mcp-server:

  https://github.com/negm17111995/mcp-server
  commit 6478de2d093fcf9bdd3c5dbff6d6ef267dcb56ae
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 MAQAMI LLC (Ahmed Nejm) (LICENSE)

The plugin was a portable manifest (plugin.json, mcp.json) plus a Node stdio
bridge (index.js) that forwarded every MCP request to MAQAMI's hosted
Streamable HTTP endpoint at https://mcp.maqami.co/, and the bundled
maqami-travel-booking skill. The endpoint needs no key, and the tool list is
the server's own. This rewrite keeps the endpoint and what a user gets from it:
one JSON-RPC POST per call, an answer read from a JSON body or from the
server-sent events the endpoint sends, the session header kept for the requests
after initialize, and the booking skill carried as the manual topic (help
:maqami) whose one line rides every request. The two tools it registers are the
bridge's two verbs -- list the server's tools, call one -- because the server
defines the list. What was left out: the Node process and the MCP SDK it drove,
the plugin's MAQAMI_MCP_URL override (the section's base_url replaces it), the
other client manifests the repository carries, and its Node test of the
forwarder, which this cell's stubbed tests replace. Nothing of the original is
vendored.
